<programme start="20261114053000 +0000" stop="20261114070000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">Saturdays In the South: A History of SEC Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Part Eight: 2010-Present</sub-title><desc lang="en">The SEC has a run of seven straight national titles, and nine in 12 years. Expansion in 2012 gives the conference 14 schools. Meanwhile, Nick Saban arguably becomes the greatest coach in the history of college football.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p17173425_b_v11_ac.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261114070000 +0000" stop="20261114100000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Houston at Colorado</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Colorado Buffaloes clash with the No. 17 Houston Cougars in Big 12 play. Colorado looks to defend its home turf following a 20-10 loss to Arizona State, while Houston relies on a 19.8 defensive scoring average to secure a conference road victory.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261114100000 +0000" stop="20261114130000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Florida State at Pittsburgh</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Pittsburgh Panthers meet the Florida State Seminoles. Pittsburgh (6-3) looks to build on on five sacks in a 34-11 win over Georgia Tech, while 4-5 Florida State is bolstered by two key interceptions in a 31-24 victory over Boston College.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
